        "comments": "The assembly of Lepidorhombus whiffiagonis (fLepWhi1) is based on 41X ONT data and Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr).The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT assembly generation with Nextdenovo, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. In total, no contigs were identified as contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral). Additionally, 28 regions totaling 5 Mb (with the largest being 0.799 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext.",
